# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# results/ is DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED.  Read this before adding it back.
#
# The pre-rebuild tree had `results/` in .gitignore *and* three result files
# committed. That combination is the worst of both worlds: git kept tracking
# the three stale files, but `git add results/<new>.json` after a fresh run
# silently did nothing, so a regenerated run never landed. That is a large part
# of why the committed results were months out of date while the code beneath
# them changed.
#
# Resolution: results/ is tracked. Acceptance criterion C6 requires that every
# number in the README be regenerated by a committed script writing into
# results/, and a reviewer must be able to see those artifacts in the checkout
# without re-running a multi-hour experiment. Regenerated results are therefore
# expected to show up as a diff -- that diff IS the reproducibility signal.
#
# Large binary by-products (checkpoints, tensors, HF caches) are excluded
# individually below; only small text/JSON/PNG artifacts belong in git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Byte-compiled / optimized
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Packaging / build
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
*.egg
dist/
build/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.env

# Testing / coverage
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
junit*.xml

# Reproducibility check scratch output (make repro-check)
.repro/

# Local caches: HuggingFace datasets/models, tokenizers, etc.
# Resolved by sca.utils.paths.cache_dir(); never commit anything from here.
.cache/
.hf_cache/

# Model weights and other large binaries. These must not enter git even when
# they land under results/.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.npy
*.npz
*.parquet
*.arrow
checkpoints/
results/**/*.pt
results/**/*.pth
results/**/*.bin
results/**/*.safetensors
results/**/*.npz

# Experiment tracking
wandb/
mlruns/
lightning_logs/

# Logs and editor/OS noise
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
